an for  the international leasing companies  they're going to lose money of course  because these these aircraft are sitting  on the ground in russia and they they  can't get to them  it is a major challenge one way or  another and  the thing is  we can only look at the unfolding um  impact of the sanctions and so on but it  is clearly one of the  major impacts that will be seen in  russia among russian air travelers  realizing you can't fly as easily or as  cheaply as you did before  and it will mean that for example the  middle eastern airlines who do fly to  russia will actually have a significant  captive market  we lost a lot of airlines uh due to the  pandemic it just wasn't survivable for  for many of the smaller airlines or  those running on on very tight  operational budgets um  with this continuing agony now with the  the the airspace restrictions around  russia with the increasing fuel prices  do you think that that we're likely to  see other airlines going under  it's going to increase the pressures  ultimately it's really what the impact  on individual countries gdp is because  it's its gdp and the ability of people  to buy tickets effectively that drives  the airline business forward and one of  the concerns is the impact in terms of  gdp growth will actually reduce  aviation growth as well but you know  none of these things are positive is the  basic point all looking at a little  bleak at the moment to say the least  peter but anyway thank you i really  appreciate you outlining all of that for  us uh peter morris there in london thank  you  now food shortages power cuts and long  lines for expensive fuel sri lanka is  facing its worst economic crisis since  independence in 1948. international  rating agencies are warning that it's on  the verge of defaulting on its debts but  the government has refused to seek an  imf bailout and insist that it can  handle the crisis on its own al  jazeera's menel fernandez reports from  colombo  spending hours in qu